      "css": ".ds-tabs{display:flex;background:#fff;height:68px;padding-top:6px;box-shadow:0 8px 18px rgba(59,42,140,.14);width:335px}.ds-tabs a{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:2px;color:#5F5A80;font:600 11px system-ui,sans-serif;text-decoration:none}.ds-tabs a.on{color:#3730A3}.ds-tabs a:active{opacity:.7}.ds-tabs a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #4F46E5;outline-offset:2px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Violet Stage",
    "overview": "Every tab opens on a violet-to-indigo gradient header that holds the one peso figure that matters, set large in Figtree with its centavos at half size. Below the stage, the work sits on a lavender-tinted canvas in white rounded cards lifted by a soft violet shadow, never outlined. Colour carries meaning: indigo for action and the active state, teal-green for income, coral-red for expense, and a hashed per-category hue on every category tile.\n\nOne design ships to Android and iOS through Expo (React Native + NativeWind v4); light and dark follow the phone. All values below are read from `frontend/src/lib/theme.ts`, `frontend/tailwind.config.js`, `frontend/src/global.css` and `frontend/src/components/ui/index.tsx`. Review captures exist only for react-native-web at 375x812 (`.impeccable/review/`); no native captures exist, so native shadow, elevation and font-fallback rendering are unverified. The gradient header is the user's explicit choice (recorded 2026-11-23). There are no shipping raster assets; every icon is an Ionicons glyph.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Gradient stage header on every tab and pushed screen; content below on canvas.",
      "Borderless white cards (24px corners) with a soft violet lift.",
      "Peso figures in Figtree 800/700 with tabular numerals; small centavos on display figures.",
      "Pills everywhere a control or progress needs a shape: buttons, segmented, chips, progress, FAB.",
      "Category identity by colour: rounded-square tiles, solid or softly tinted."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Stage-Only Gradient Rule",
        "body": "The gradient appears only behind headers (and the pinned status-bar scrim). Content surfaces are flat canvas and card colours.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Money Has a Colour Rule",
        "body": "Income is always `income` with a `+`, expense always `expense` with a `-`; neutral totals stay `fg`. Use `Money` or `BigMoney`, never colour a peso figure by hand.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token-Only Rule",
        "body": "Classes read colours through CSS variables (`bg-card`, `text-fg`, `bg-brand-light`, `text-brand-dark`); props that need a raw value read `usePalette()`. No hex literals in screens, except `#FFFFFF` on brand or gradient.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Money Rule",
        "body": "Every peso figure uses tabular numerals (`DISPLAY`, `FIGURE`, or the `tabular-nums` variant in `Money`/`PillBar`) so columns line up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Scales-With-The-Phone Rule",
        "body": "Text follows the system font size. Cap scaling (`maxFontSizeMultiplier`) only inside fixed-size cells, and put the full value in the accessibility label.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Border Card Rule",
        "body": "Cards separate from the canvas by colour and lift, never by an outline. Borders belong to inputs, chips, dashed Empty states and in-card row dividers.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** start a new screen with `Screen` and a header built from `GradientHeader` (tabs) or `StackHeader` (pushed routes); put content in `Card`s on the canvas.",
      "**Do** show peso amounts with `BigMoney`, `Money` or `FIGURE`, so they keep tabular numerals and income/expense colouring.",
      "**Do** take colours from tailwind tokens or `usePalette()`, and check the screen in both light and dark.",
      "**Do** give every control `accessibilityRole` and label, a 48px minimum target, and an `active:` press class.",
      "**Do** colour categories with `categoryColor(name)` through `CategoryTile`, never a hand-picked hue.",
      "**Do** keep one primary action per screen; when it is \"add\", it is the FAB."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put the gradient on cards, buttons or the canvas; it is the stage only.",
      "**Don't** outline cards or add a second shadow style; use `lift`.",
      "**Don't** use square or small-radius corners on controls; controls are pills, containers 16-24px.",
      "**Don't** set money in the system face or with proportional digits.",
      "**Don't** use `dark:` classes; dark values come from the CSS variables set at the root (`darkMode: 'class'` is only there to keep NativeWind web from crashing)."
    ]
  }
}
